# Yarn v1 enforces the package.json "engines" range on EVERY `yarn <script>`
# (yarn dev, yarn build, yarn test, ...), aborting with a generic message before
# any of our own scripts run. We keep "engines" for documentation and for npm,
# but let the targeted scripts/check-node.js guard (wired as pretest / preunit)
# emit the clear, test-specific Node message instead of yarn's blunt, all-command
# block. See scripts/check-node.js and the pinned version in .nvmrc.
ignore-engines true
